From b5f677205bc711316cbbc98d7906e5b8328f072c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:31:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): pickup import certifies a card's containment
 receipts from the replica; one refused card no longer aborts the batch
 [daveey]

Problem: 06:28Z-08:35Z Nov 20 every worker-1 pickup failed (~every 17 s) with
sqlite3.IntegrityError: containment_pending at import_cards -> apply_remote_changes
-> _apply_one -> _upsert_row (INSERT), so no pool card was imported while ~67 waited.

Why 1: the INSERT of a released card's `contained`/`containment_released` task_events
row hits trigger containment_event_insert, which allows it only when
kanban_containment_sync_event -> replica.event_permit finds a matching receipt in the
live file's containment_canonical_receipts cache.
Why 2: that cache is filled only by certify_page (sync loop, Hub evidence). Pickup
copies replica -> live without the Hub and never called it, so the live cache had no
receipt for the copied card's events (the replica file does: its own pull certified them).
Why 3: import_cards applied every picked card in ONE apply_remote_changes transaction,
so the single refused row rolled back all cards, and pickup retried the same batch each tick.
Root (happened): the pickup copy path was added before containment receipts existed and
nothing made it follow the same certification rule as the feed path.
Root (not caught): no test ran pickup with the real containment triggers and a released card.
Recurrence: PR #3753 (receipt cache ignores re-stamp bookkeeping) fixed a different refusal
(canonical receipt identity changed) on the sync path; this path was untouched.

Fix: replica.adopt_receipts re-certifies each protected event's receipt (stored in the
replica's cache) into the live cache with remember() (signature, board, origin, stop/release
pair) and checks the event equals it, offline. import_cards does this per card; a card that
cannot be certified is left out (never by disabling a trigger), logged with its id and table
(task_events), and recorded as a kanban_pickup_skips row (reason other); the rest import.
Guard triggers are unchanged.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_containment_import.py (real triggers): RED on
base (IntegrityError containment_pending), GREEN with fix; 66 related test files pass.
